{"judgments": [
 {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The recital of the Trust's purpose — a \"continuous source of managed investment for cash collateral\" for securities lenders — is argued to control the far broader operative investment latitude granted in the Portfolio Diversification list (c031) and the authority to place all assets in another series (c044). Whether this stated purpose limits those operative powers is a live construction question.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.27},
   {"issue": "The offer is described as made \"to qualified institutional purchasers,\" which does not square with the cover legend's \"qualified institutional or accredited investors\" or with the \"qualified purchasers\" of Section 3(c)(7) relied on in c055 and the Subscription Agreement's accredited-investor/qualified-purchaser representations. Which eligibility standard governs admission is left unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Shareholders become entitled to share in income and gains \"upon acceptance of their subscriptions ... and payment of the consideration specified by Wells Fargo from time to time,\" which cannot be squared with the fixed $10.00 initial price in c007 or with Declaration of Trust Section 4.5 crediting investments at the Net Asset Value next determined. The price at which subscriptions are taken is therefore indeterminate.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.19}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Wells Fargo's self-appointment as investment manager, with power to retain affiliated advisers, sits against Declaration of Trust Section 6.1, which bars any contract retaining the Trustee or its affiliates for additional services for additional compensation beyond that disclosed and agreed in the securities lending agreements. Whether the self-appointment is permitted, and on what compensation, must be construed across the two documents.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.23}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"The specific portion advised by any of these investment advisers will vary from time to time in the sole discretion of Wells Fargo\" supplies no standard, notice or limit on delegation. The provision is standardless as to how much of the portfolio may be handed to a sub-adviser.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.13}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c006", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Each Share is said to represent \"an undivided proportionate interest in all assets and liabilities of the CI Term Trust,\" whereas Declaration of Trust Section 4.6 makes each Share an equal undivided interest in the net assets of the Series \"except to the extent affected by expense allocations.\" The unqualified statement here and the qualified one there cannot both be given full effect.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.18}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c007", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c008", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c009", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Shares are offered \"at the then applicable value per Share (as defined below),\" but no definition of \"value per Share\" appears anywhere below in the Memorandum. The cross-reference is broken, leaving the purchase price term undefined.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c010", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The minimum initial investment is \"determined by Wells Fargo in the efficient management of the securities lending and investment program\" — a garbled phrase supplying no ascertainable standard or amount. \"Efficient management\" has no measurable content as a criterion for a minimum subscription.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c011", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Valuing assets \"each Business Day at their then current market value\" cannot be squared with c029's objective of maintaining a stable $10.00 price per Share, which presupposes amortized-cost valuation, nor with Declaration of Trust Section 5.3's Net Asset Value determined \"in a manner consistent with the 1940 Act.\" Which valuation basis governs redemptions and subscriptions is unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.31}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c012", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The mandatory daily declaration and monthly payment of dividends conflicts with Declaration of Trust Section 5.1, which leaves the amount, timing and form of any distribution wholly to the Trustee's discretion. Whether Shareholders have an enforceable entitlement to a daily dividend turns on which text controls.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.15}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c013", "issues": [
